 the eventual Republican nominee or a divisive GOP primary could narrow the margin, though Wyoming becoming genuinely competitive remains a remote scenario.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Wyoming remains the most Republican-leaning state in the country, and the presidential race there reflects that. A partisan lean of roughly twenty-three points in the Republicans' favor anchors the forecast, with no incumbent advantage in play and no state polls or expert ratings yet published to suggest otherwise. National headlines point to a difficult environment for Republicans, including voter discontent and Democratic gains heading into the 2026 midterms, but nothing state-specific indicates Wyoming is moving.\n\nWithout polling, uncertainty is wide, and a strong national swing could trim the Republican margin by a few points. Even so, Wyoming has not backed a Democrat for president in decades, and the structural lean is large enough that the race is rated Safe Republican. The main question is the size of the Republican victory, not the winner.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.01, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0232, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0282, "margin": -22.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.025, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0274, "margin": -22.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0226, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0236, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0279, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0235, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0258, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0202, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0256, "margin": -